 "result": "Call order at the end of a request:\n\n1. `Tessel.finalize_request` (`src/tessel/app.py:1021`) calls `make_response(rv)` to build the response, then calls `finalize_reply`.\n2. `Tessel.finalize_reply` (`src/tessel/app.py:1394`) runs the `after_request` functions, then calls `session_interface.is_null_session(...)`. If the session isn't null, it calls `persist_session`.\n3. `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session` (`src/tessel/sessions.py:337`) is the default session interface's implementation.\n   - It reads the cookie settings via `get_cookie_name`, `get_cookie_domain`, `get_cookie_path`, `get_cookie_secure`, `get_cookie_partitioned`, `get_cookie_samesite` and `get_cookie_httponly`.\n   - If the session was modified to be empty, it calls `response.delete_cookie(...)`.\n   - Otherwise `cookie_needs_write` (`sessions.py:233`) decides whether to write. It returns true if the session was modified, or if it is permanent and `SESSION_REFRESH_EACH_REQUEST` is set.\n   - It then gets the expiry from `get_expiration_time` and the signed value from `make_signer(app).dumps(dict(session))`, and writes the cookie with `response.set_cookie(...)` (`sessions.py:374`).\n\nThe abstract `SessionInterface.persist_session` is at `sessions.py:263`.",
